<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Elijah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">9th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century-bce">9th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Elijah was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew">Hebrew</a> prophet of the 9th century BCE in the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-israel">Kingdom of Israel</a>, known from the biblical Books of Kings. He opposed King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahab">Ahab</a> and Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jezebel">Jezebel</a> and their promotion of the worship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baal">Baal</a>, most famously in the contest on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-carmel">Mount Carmel</a>, and was said to have been taken up to heaven in a whirlwind. He is honoured in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judaism">Judaism</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/elijah.jpg" alt="Elijah" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giovanni Girolamo Savoldo · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Giovanni_Girolamo_Savoldo,_Elijah_Fed_by_the_Raven,_c._1510,_NGA_46134.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
